<Base title="GATE 2027 application guide (GOAPS)" description="How GATE 2027 registration works: GOAPS, DigiLocker for Indian nationals, rectification window, and mistakes to avoid." canonicalPath="/gate-2027/application/">
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Editorial guide · official portal is authoritative</p>
    <h1>GATE 2027 application guide</h1>
    <p class="lead">Registration runs through GOAPS. For GATE 2027, registration through DigiLocker is mandatory for Indian nationals. Apply early — the rectification window (14–21 Oct 2026) only fixes limited fields.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap grid cols-2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Steps</h3><ol><li>Create/verify your DigiLocker account (Indian nationals).</li><li>Register on GOAPS after 2 Sep 2026.</li><li>Fill personal, academic and paper details carefully.</li><li>Upload photo, signature and certificates per spec.</li><li>Pay before the regular deadline (27 Sep 2026) to avoid late fees.</li><li>Save the enrolment ID and check email/SMS for defects.</li></ol></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Avoid these mistakes</h3><ul><li>Waiting until the extended deadline (5 Oct 2026) and hitting server load.</li><li>Wrong paper code or exam city order.</li><li>Blurry photo / wrong file size.</li><li>Name mismatch with DigiLocker / ID.</li><li>Assuming the rectification window fixes everything — it doesn't.</li></ul></div>
  </div></section>
